# EtListItem V2

## Purpose

Generic slot-based list item container for the eToro design system. Uses a flexible compound component pattern with Start/Middle/End content slots, an optional Divider, and a standalone Skeleton.

For swipe-to-reveal actions, wrap `EtListItemV2` with `EtSwipeableRow` (see below).

## Architecture

```text
et-list-item.tsx (main) → provides ListItemContext, single render path
├── EtListItem.Start    → reads context for flex behavior, default left-aligned
├── EtListItem.Middle   → reads context, default centered (3-slot mode only)
├── EtListItem.End      → reads context for flex behavior, default right-aligned
├── EtListItem.Divider  → hairline separator, composed as a child (no context needed)
└── EtListItem.Skeleton → skeleton loading placeholder, composed as a child (inherits size from parent)

EtSwipeableRow (public, standalone) → wraps any content to add swipe-to-reveal actions
└── EtSwipeableRow.Action → action button subcomponents revealed on left swipe
```

### Slot Detection

Slots are identified at runtime via a static `__SLOT_TYPE` property on each compound component (not `displayName`). Static properties survive minification, unlike `displayName` which is a debugging aid only.

```tsx
// Each compound component has:
ListItemStart.__SLOT_TYPE = 'start';
ListItemMiddle.__SLOT_TYPE = 'middle';
ListItemEnd.__SLOT_TYPE = 'end';
ListItemDivider.__SLOT_TYPE = 'divider';
ListItemSkeleton.__SLOT_TYPE = 'skeleton';

// useListItemChildren reads __SLOT_TYPE to classify children
const getSlotType = (child: ReactNode): SlotType | undefined =>
  isValidElement(child) ? (child.type as { __SLOT_TYPE?: SlotType }).__SLOT_TYPE : undefined;
```

### Single Render Path

The root component has two render paths based on children:

1. **Skeleton mode** – when `EtListItem.Skeleton` is a child, only the skeleton is rendered. Size, style, and testID are inherited from the parent `EtListItem` unless explicitly set on the skeleton.
2. **Slot mode** – a column `View` containing a row of slots, plus an optional divider below. When `EtListItem.Divider` is present as a child, the container uses `paddingTop` only (divider sits at the bottom edge); otherwise `paddingVertical` applies normally.

## API

### Props

| Prop                 | Type                   | Default   | Description                                               |
| -------------------- | ---------------------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| `children`           | `EtListItemChildren`   | -         | Compound children (Start, Middle, End, Divider, Skeleton) |
| `size`               | `'large' \| 'small'`   | `'large'` | Vertical padding size                                     |
| `style`              | `StyleProp<ViewStyle>` | -         | Container style override                                  |
| `onPress`            | `() => void`           | -         | Press handler; renders content as Pressable when set      |
| `disabled`           | `boolean`              | `false`   | Dims the row (0.5 opacity), suppresses `onPress`, and sets `accessibilityState.disabled` |
| `testID`             | `string`               | -         | Test ID                                                   |
| `accessibilityLabel` | `string`               | -         | Accessibility label (used when onPress is set)            |

### Slot Subcomponents

Each content slot accepts `children`, `style`, and `testID` props.

| Slot     | Default Alignment   | 2-Slot Flex     | 3-Slot Flex |
| -------- | ------------------- | --------------- | ----------- |
| `Start`  | `flex-start` (left) | `flex: 1`       | `flex: 1`   |
| `Middle` | `center`            | N/A             | `flex: 1`   |
| `End`    | `flex-end` (right)  | `flexShrink: 0` | `flex: 1`   |

### EtListItem.Divider

Hairline separator rendered below the slot row. Accepts `style` and `testID` props.

### EtListItem.Skeleton

Compound subcomponent for skeleton loading states. Must be used within `EtListItem`. Inherits `size`, `style`, and `testID` from the parent unless explicitly overridden. Does not use ListItemContext.

| Prop      | Type                                                         | Default   | Description              |
| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | --------- | ------------------------ |
| `variant` | `'1-line' \| '2-lines' \| 'asset-1-line' \| 'asset-2-lines'` | -         | Skeleton layout variant  |
| `size`    | `'large' \| 'small'`                                         | `'large'` | Vertical padding size    |
| `style`   | `StyleProp<ViewStyle>`                                       | -         | Container style override |
| `testID`  | `string`                                                     | -         | Test ID                  |

Skeleton variants:

- `'1-line'` - Single bar left + small bar right
- `'2-lines'` - Two bars left + one bar right
- `'asset-1-line'` - Small square + bar left + small bar right
- `'asset-2-lines'` - Large square + two bars left + bar right

## Swipe-to-Reveal Actions

Use `EtSwipeableRow` from `etoro-ui` to add swipe actions to any content. Place the content element first, then compose `EtSwipeableRow.Action` subcomponents as direct children after it.

```tsx
import { EtListItemV2, EtSwipeableRow } from 'etoro-ui';

<EtSwipeableRow
  isDragging={isAnyItemDragging}
  onSwipeStart={(close) => {
    if (activeCloseRef.current && activeCloseRef.current !== close) {
      activeCloseRef.current();
    }
    activeCloseRef.current = close;
  }}
>
  <EtListItemV2 onPress={handleNavigate} accessibilityLabel="AAPL">
    <EtListItemV2.Start>
      <AssetInfo />
    </EtListItemV2.Start>
    <EtListItemV2.Middle>
      <SparkChart />
    </EtListItemV2.Middle>
    <EtListItemV2.End>
      <PriceDisplay />
    </EtListItemV2.End>
    <EtListItemV2.Divider />
  </EtListItemV2>
  <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={handleTrade} style={{ backgroundColor: '#4ECDC4' }} accessibilityLabel="Trade">
    <TradeIcon />
  </EtSwipeableRow.Action>
  <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={handleRemove} style={{ backgroundColor: '#FF6B6B' }} width={80} accessibilityLabel="Delete">
    <TrashIcon />
  </EtSwipeableRow.Action>
</EtSwipeableRow>;
```

### EtSwipeableRow Props

| Prop                    | Type                               | Default | Description                                         |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `children`              | `ReactNode`                        | -       | Content element followed by Action subcomponents    |
| `isDragging`            | `boolean`                          | -       | Whether parent list is dragging (auto-closes swipe) |
| `onSwipeStart`          | `(closeSwipe: () => void) => void` | -       | Called when swipe starts; receives close function   |
| `contentContainerStyle` | `StyleProp<ViewStyle>`             | -       | Style applied to the sliding content container      |

### EtSwipeableRow.Action Props

| Prop                 | Type                   | Default | Description                                       |
| -------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `children`           | `ReactNode`            | -       | Content rendered inside the action                |
| `onPress`            | `() => void`           | -       | Called when tapped; swipe auto-closes after press |
| `width`              | `number`               | `70`    | Width in pixels; affects total snap distance      |
| `style`              | `StyleProp<ViewStyle>` | -       | Container style (use backgroundColor)             |
| `accessibilityLabel` | `string`               | -       | Accessibility label for screen readers            |

## Layout Rules

1. **Start only** - Start slot takes full width (flex: 1), left-aligned
2. **Start + End** - content-based widths (Start flex: 1, End sizes to content), **12px gap (X3)**
3. **Start + Middle + End** - equal width distribution (all flex: 1), **8px gap (X2)**
4. **Divider** - when `EtListItem.Divider` is a child, renders below slots with size-based spacing

## Usage Examples

```tsx
// Start only
<EtListItem size="large">
  <EtListItem.Start><MyContent /></EtListItem.Start>
</EtListItem>

// Start + End with divider
<EtListItem size="small">
  <EtListItem.Start><Label>Name</Label></EtListItem.Start>
  <EtListItem.End><Price>$186.79</Price></EtListItem.End>
  <EtListItem.Divider />
</EtListItem>

// Start + Middle + End (equal widths)
<EtListItem size="large">
  <EtListItem.Start><Col1 /></EtListItem.Start>
  <EtListItem.Middle><Col2 /></EtListItem.Middle>
  <EtListItem.End><Col3 /></EtListItem.End>
</EtListItem>

// Checkbox variant (composition)
<EtListItem size="large">
  <EtListItem.Start><SettingLabel /></EtListItem.Start>
  <EtListItem.End><EtCheckbox value={on} onChange={toggle} /></EtListItem.End>
  <EtListItem.Divider />
</EtListItem>

// Toggle variant (composition)
<EtListItem size="large" style={selected && { backgroundColor: 'rgba(204,204,204,0.15)' }}>
  <EtListItem.Start><SettingLabel /></EtListItem.Start>
  <EtListItem.End><EtToggle value={on} onChange={toggle} /></EtListItem.End>
  <EtListItem.Divider />
</EtListItem>

// Skeleton loading
<EtListItem size="large">
  <EtListItem.Skeleton variant="asset-2-lines" />
</EtListItem>
```

## Anti-Patterns

- **Do NOT** use `displayName` for slot detection logic — use `__SLOT_TYPE` static property instead. `displayName` is for DevTools only.
- **Do NOT** use `EtListItem.Middle` without also providing `Start` and `End`
- **Do NOT** nest `EtListItem` inside another `EtListItem`
- **Do NOT** use subcomponents outside of `EtListItem` (slots will throw, skeleton must be composed as a child)
- **Do NOT** use `EtListItem.Skeleton` as a standalone component — always wrap it in `<EtListItem>`
- **Do NOT** put layout/flex styles on the root when using slots (use slot `style` prop instead)
- **Do NOT** add boolean props that create branching render paths — compose with compound subcomponents instead
- **Do NOT** add swipe props directly to `EtListItemV2` — use `EtSwipeableRow` as a wrapper instead
- **Do NOT** wrap `EtListItemV2` in a raw `Pressable` when using `EtSwipeableRow` — swipe gestures conflict. Use the `onPress` prop on `EtListItemV2` instead

## Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - for divider colors
- Spacing constants: `X2`, `X3`, `X4`, `X6` from `core/styles/spacing`
- `EtSkeleton` - for skeleton shimmer animation
- No additional third-party dependencies (all entries above are internal components/utilities)

## Design System Integration

`EtListItem` is a structural compound component — `Start`, `Middle`, `End`, and `Skeleton` slots don't apply explicit color tokens (consumers compose their own content). The only theme color the component itself reads is for the divider:

| Slot | V2 token |
| --- | --- |
| `EtListItem.Divider` ([`list-item-divider.tsx`](libs/etoro-ui/src/components/list/list-item-v2/subcomponents/list-item-divider.tsx)) | `carbonSecondaryDivider` (matches Figma's `var(--primary-divider)` hex `#B2B2B226`) |

### Behavior delta (V1 → V2)

The strict-Figma migration to V2 (`38622:337490`) introduced one user-visible change:

- **Divider hue** flips from a solid neutral (`dividerSenary` — `#F2F2F2` light / `#333333` dark) to a translucent grey (`carbonSecondaryDivider` — `#B2B2B226`, both modes). Visually similar on plain backgrounds; reads as a translucent overlay on busier surfaces. Identical to the divider treatment now in `EtAssetItem` — the two list components share the same divider hex.
